    "status": "SUPPORTED",
    "observed_function": "forms a cylinder of 14 subunits composed of two heptameric rings stacked back-to-back (pubmed:1361169, pubmed:15327959, pubmed:7935790, pubmed:8846220, pubmed:9285585). interacts with the co-chaperonin groes (pubmed:1361169, pubmed:25174333, pubmed:7638600, pubmed:7638601, pubmed:8618836, pubmed:8663256, pubmed:9285585). can form asymmetrical complexes, composed of one groel and one groes, and symmetrical complexes, formed between one groel and two groes oligomers (pubmed:1361169, pubmed:25174333, pubmed:7638600, pubmed:7638601, pubmed:8618836, pubmed:8663256). the asymmetrical complex is the functional unit (pubmed:25912285, pubmed:7638600, pubmed:7638601). it was suggested that the symmetric heterooligomer may represent a transient intermediate in the chaperonin protein folding cycle (pubmed:8618836, pubmed:8663256). another study shows that the symmetric heterooligomers are substantially populated only in the presence of proteins that cannot be folded by the chaperonin (pubmed:25912285)",
